      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:10 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Laura Peter, Deputy Director, Patent and Trademark Office)",
      "case_id": "2019-18-801",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6503ebbc1877ebed1ad4b842a3f8dc5e9547dd483c01b755f9ec7a4476fafad0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6503ebbc1877-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "An unsuccessful patent applicant may seek judicial review through either a direct appeal to the Federal Circuit under 35 U.S.C. 141 or a district court suit under Section 145. Section 145 states that an applicant who files suit under that provision must pay all the expenses of the proceeding."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE GINSBURG",
      "case_id": "2019-18-801",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6503ebbc1877ebed1ad4b842a3f8dc5e9547dd483c01b755f9ec7a4476fafad0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6503ebbc1877-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Stewart, do you dispute the Federal Circuit's estimate that if this cost of the PTO attorneys is spread among all patent applicants, even the ones who don't use 145, that the added cost per applicant would be $1.60?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Heritage Reporting Corporation",
      "case_id": "2019-18-801",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6503ebbc1877ebed1ad4b842a3f8dc5e9547dd483c01b755f9ec7a4476fafad0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6503ebbc1877-0001-0007",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Bouvier Legal Dictionary define \"expensae litis,\" which literally means expenses of litigation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2019-18-801",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6503ebbc1877ebed1ad4b842a3f8dc5e9547dd483c01b755f9ec7a4476fafad0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6503ebbc1877-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Okay. And in your experience, where you're settling out of court or where you're -- you're trying to work out a system without going into court for resolving a claimant who says this is infringing my patent, or there are all kinds of people claiming it, you set up private systems, and the private systems, whether it's arbitration, mediation, thousands of different systems, involve costs, is it fairly common, not fairly common, unheard of, or what, to say in the contract that, it's doing this for future controversies, that you bring up the controversy, you pay the whole thing? Or maybe the opposite. What's it like?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Chu",
      "case_id": "2019-18-801",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6503ebbc1877ebed1ad4b842a3f8dc5e9547dd483c01b755f9ec7a4476fafad0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6503ebbc1877-0002-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. CHU: I can think of no instance by my personal experience or through reading or otherwise where a contract would say you bring this up and you pay for the whole thing, no matter what, including attorneys' fees."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2019-18-801",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6503ebbc1877ebed1ad4b842a3f8dc5e9547dd483c01b755f9ec7a4476fafad0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6503ebbc1877-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "government argued that there is no other statute that would be affected."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2019-18-801",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6503ebbc1877ebed1ad4b842a3f8dc5e9547dd483c01b755f9ec7a4476fafad0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6503ebbc1877-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: I think this goes back to a question that you got at the very beginning. But setting attorneys' fees aside, could you tell us, Mr. Stewart, exactly what expenses you charge for and exactly what expenses you don't?"
    },
